Risks Related to Our Business
We operate in a very competitive industry and may not be able to maintain our revenue and profitability.
Since the 1990s, several international companies engaged in supplying integrated automation services for the petroleum extraction industry have been qualified in China. These competitors have significantly greater financial and marketing resources and name recognition than we have. In addition, at least five domestic private competitors also compete with us, and more competitors may enter the market as Chinese petroleum companies seek to reduce oil production costs and improve efficiencies. There can be no assurance that we will be able to compete effectively in our industry.
In addition, our competitors may introduce new systems. If these new systems are more attractive to customers than the systems we currently use or may develop, our customers may switch to our competitors’ services, and we may lose market share. We believe that competition may become more intense as more integrated automation service providers, including Chinese/foreign joint ventures, are qualified to conduct business. We cannot assure you that we will be able to compete successfully against any new or existing competitors, or against any new systems our competitors may implement. Any of these competitive factors could have a material adverse effect on our revenue and profitability.
Our waste plastic chemical recycling business is in an early stage of development and involves new technologies, substantial capital expenditures, regulatory approvals and uncertain commercialization.
We are developing a waste plastic chemical recycling business in Weifang, Shandong Province, through Recon-SD. The project is designed to process 40,000 tons of low-value waste plastics per year and produce approximately 30,000 tons of plastic pyrolysis oil and 6,000 tons of carbon residue annually. This business is new to us and is in the initial stage of trial production and commissioning, having commenced trial production on September 28, 2026. Our ability to successfully commercialize this business is subject to numerous risks and uncertainties, including:
- our limited operating history and experience in the chemical recycling industry, and our ability to ramp up the plant from trial production to stable commercial production at expected yields, utilization rates and product quality;
- our dependence on obtaining and maintaining all approvals, permits and qualifications required for production, and the risk that changes in environmental, safety or industry regulations may require additional approvals or expenditures;
- our ability to secure a stable and sufficient supply of waste plastics feedstock at acceptable prices, and the risk that feedstock collection, sorting or contamination issues may disrupt production;
- the price and market acceptance of our plastic pyrolysis oil, including our ability to obtain and maintain ISCC (International Sustainability and Carbon Certification) certification and to sell the pyrolysis oil as sustainable feedstock to domestic and international customers;
- our dependence on third-party technology partners and equipment suppliers for key process technology, and the risk that such partners fail to perform or that we are unable to maintain access to the technology;
- the concentration of a material portion of our investment in a single plant in Shandong, and the risk that construction, commissioning or operational issues at that plant could materially and adversely affect the entire project;
- competition from established petrochemical, environmental and chemical recycling companies, many of which have greater financial, technical and market resources than we have;
- the significant capital expenditures required to complete and operate the plant, and the risk that we may not obtain sufficient financing on acceptable terms; and
- the uncertainty that this new business will generate revenue or profitability, and the risk that the value of the related assets may be impaired if the business does not develop as planned.
